# Direct dependencies with their allowed range – the foundation for tools/lock.py.
# Rule: within the major version (before 1.0: within the minor version). The weekly security update only picks
# versions inside these ranges; leaving a range (e.g. Flask 4) is a deliberate change made here.
# Installation always uses requirements.txt – there ALL packages including sub-dependencies are pinned to an exact
# version with SHA-256 hashes.
